{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations","id":1339693,"title":"What artefacts have you taken? What fun did you have with their evocations?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-05T13:57:37-07:00","id":1339693,"title":"What artefacts have you taken? What fun did you have with their evocations?","content":"(This is about Evocation sets, not &quot;I took a jade breastplate&quot; or whatever)<br /> <br /> Despite me and several of my players owning Arms of the Chosen, I've rarely seen anyone actually use any evocations. Many of the PCs have artefact weapons, but they're pretty generic orichalcum daiklaives or staffs or whatever they took when the game started, before these books came out with more options, so I haven't seen Evocations used much. There's a few with cool backstories (like the Walrus-totem's grimcleaver made of his own tusk), but as they're not from the books, they don't have a fully-realised set of evocations.<br /> (There's also some stuff they took from dead Dragonblood, that as ST I picked from the books, like Rainwalker, Shining Ice Mirror, etc. But they traded them back for peace/threw down the back of the sofa and forgot about them. But they didn't use them.)<br /> <br /> My friend's theo-fascist Dawn warlord has Five Edicts Dominion, which mostly seems to involve people attacking him and then falling over prone while he laughs contemptuously.<br /> I had Godspeed Vanguard, which was pretty cool; you could sneak around invisibly which is quite entertaining as a 30ft golden golem. Though sadly I didn't get to use it much.<br /> That's pretty much it.<br /> <br /> So I'd like to hear from you; what evocation sets have you taken? What fun have you had with the Evocations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T14:12:27-07:00","id":1339695,"title":"","content":"The only player that had an artifact in a game of mine had the Eternal Pyre, which was a Red Jade Daiklave who burned with the blood of its enemies as fuel (gaining power as it dealt decisive damage or hit a battle group), who could use the increasing bonfire to activate evocations like throwing the fire at enemies at short range in a gust of flame, or increased decisive damage who created a bonfire, and things like that. It was cool, but I don\u00b4t keep evocations because we wrote them on paper, and who knows where the paper is.<br /> <br /> My current character has the Silver-Skinned Hauberk, Moonsilver tattoos who shine when she is struck, creating a kind of dissonant force who repels weapon (so, justifying light artifact armor stats in what are a bunch of tattoos :P) but we haven\u00b4t write Evocations for it her because we only have had time for a single session. The only thing we know is that they can\u00b4t be deattuned unless removed by Medicine in a hard procedure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:37:51-07:00","id":1339715,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm not sure if this counts, but I once had one of my player's Dawns challenge a powerful Dragonblooded queen to a duel and by the grace of Shining Ice Mirror she actually won, without any of the DB charms in the book even because it hadn't come out yet. Now, it's true she was using the Solar evocations for SIM but, I think having almost no native charms kind of balanced that a bit. Her victory was also...really crushing. She didn't get hit even once and took down the Dawn in three attacks, in spite of a 3 die stunt on the final attack by said Dawn.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I've had much the same experience as you, most players don't even bother with attunement bonuses from what I've seen, and I'm not sure any of them have taken evocations or made their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T15:45:46-07:00","id":1339716,"title":"","content":"Of all the games I've played or gm'd there's been at least one player who invests significantly in an artifact, sometimes several. Although it's most often the more experienced players only who go for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-05T16:06:57-07:00","id":1339720,"title":"","content":"I used Sun's Brush on my Lore Supernal, which was a lot of fun flavor-wise. You haven't experienced true Solar Hubris until you've written &quot;IGNORANCE&quot; in golden letters on a giant flaming demon with the effect of lowering all their dice proportionally to how much dumber they are than you.<br /> <br /> I also had Asphodel, which basically ended up being a neat excuse for the ST to give us hints and tips in return for doing small favors for the ruler of the city inside Asphodel.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Circle mate used the Heaven and Earth Gauntlets, which are absolutely amazing power-wise. He never got to the capstone which lets you divert the course of mountains with a single punch, but the Evocations he did get saved his life more than once.<br /> <br /> That Circle mate also had the Ultimately Useful Tube, which with its 1000 uses was a perfect fit for his comic relief type character.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another Circle mate was the most unsubtle Night ever, a building-lifting Athletics Supernal who expressed her pyromania with the Sekhem flamethrower. That thing is extremely potent for Jade, and it single-handedly turned the tide of battle from a total party wipe to a total victory against Mahicara the Volcanic Earthwalker. I came out of that fight with the feeling that that Behemoth was designed for the explicit purpose of being utterly destroyed by Sehkem.<br /> <br /> <br /> A third Circle mate had Stormcaller. His player struggles with roleplaying, so we were worried he would have trouble playing with a cursed 5 dot artifact. We warned him it would have a huge impact on his character but he insisted on taking it. And then as we feared he started disliking his character when his story became centered on his relationship with the cursed blade and whether he would manage to fight its evil influence. He ended up dropping his character altogether and switching for a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T11:03:35-07:00","id":1339876,"title":"","content":"Cynis Ganan is having GREAT fun with Fist of Titans in my One-on-One-On-One-on-One game. ST is taking the whole &quot;likely destroy mundane structures if used indoors&quot; thing a little literally for my liking. But he's had great fun smashing beastmen through palace walls (and he's got Craft: Architecture) so...<br /> <br /> Mnemon Alinos Danireya is rocking Perdurant Vault after... aggressive negotiations with a Ragara auditor (sent to ensure that the Alinos family were not embezzling vast sums from their Satrapy that was due to the Realm/to pay off Ragara loans). She's not had it long, but is presently using it to investigate why the shield is yielding its Evocations as if she were a scion of the hated Ragara family. The boost to Guile from Subliminal Sanctuary has been especially useful. But she's also used it to batter a bear to death, which was pretty metal as she's Dex 3 Melee 3 with literally no Melee charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 10-16-2019, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-06T14:55:39-07:00","id":1339925,"title":"","content":"Well, my first solar character, Modest Verse, was a wandering sorcerer-exorcist partly inspired in Miroku from Inu-Yasha, so his first &quot;artifact&quot; was actually his cursed right arm, represented by Wood Dragon's Claws as control spell.<br /> <br /> Used &quot;green jade/wood magic make things grow or wither and siphon Essence from living things&quot; as an excuse to steal evocations from soulsteel artifacts like Asphodel and Soulfarer both to make my own weird set, where the arm's vague setience awareness that occasionally messed with his mind in eerie prophetic mad dreams (\u201cScarred by Nightmares\u201d archetype) would eventually evolve into full bloom (sorry) conscience, a creature living and ruling a strange dream-world of its own for which the PC's arm acted as a gate of sorts.<br /> <br /> Later on the ST pointed out those might be too powerful a set of evocations for just a terrestrial circle spell, so we made a custom occult charm or two to boost the artifact level of my control spell into 5 and leave me free rein with the crazy.<br /> <br /> (yeah, the charms did some other cool things related to thaumaturgy and occult actions, but running amok with the evocations as i alreaady did was my point all along) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For a Dragon-blooded game, i had considered making a kid that exalted in the middle of some podunk in the Isle, was turned into a sort of feral, Mowgli-esque figure and self-taught sorcerer &amp; &quot;wood gods king&quot; through a mix of essence fever, inexperience and luck, until a group of monks looking for an unruly spirit got quite a surprise but managed to restrain him and take the young feral dragon to be properly civilized through immaculate education and indoctrination with, mixed, ressults. My idea was to see him eventually turning into a literal dragon, snatching Mela's Coils set of evocations as reference for that.<br /> <br /> But then someone pointed out that &quot;bad holy man with a proclivilty for summoning and crazy shenanigans with Wood Dragon's Claws&quot; was pretty much a summary of my Solar too, so i decided to try something else.<br /> <br /> (I <i>might </i>have also decided that my follow-up idea - using Mela's Coil &quot;become a lesser elemental dragon&quot; capstone charm as a springboard for buying Warstrider charms might be <i><b>a little</b></i> too much abuse for just the control spell of a self-taught young DB. Maybe....) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Instead at present i'm divided between two concepts:<br /> - a geomancer with a passion for jewelry, hearthstones, the &quot;spirit of stones&quot; and understand why some of them could manifest evocations and others not.<br /> - a young dynast so hilariously obsessed with riches he's experimenting with &quot;jade is magic - jade is money - money is magic&quot; associations to create a arcane art he calls <i>mammonism</i> (Resources Evocations). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm almost tempted to combine them in one, if i didn't know trying to toy with two sets evocation-based magics would be a ridiculous XP drain to actually explore ingame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-06-2019, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T04:21:35-07:00","id":1340011,"title":"","content":"Quite simple because the artifact was not necessary but I punched someone out of a 30 feet tall aqueduc with Heaven And Earth Gauntlets with the appropriate evocation that reduces penalties to smash attacks (I think that's its name ? The level 3 artefact smashfist)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T08:10:45-07:00","id":1340031,"title":"","content":"I make basically bespoke artifacts for all of my players, both weapon and armor.<br /> <br /> The reason for this is primarily for theming issues. As I have particular things and ideas for stories and how I want to present them, Evocations enhance the told story and offer avenues of interpretation.<br /> <br /> For instance all of my Dragonblooded PCs in my DB game have an Evocation on either their weapon or armor that gives them the ability to launch a free Elemental Bolt attack if they execute a certain condition. This both allows the player to be rewarded for playing to their concept and let's me include themes in the artifact and how it processes. Similarly, their weapons are designed to tell a story about the DB as an individual, and strengthens those stories.<br /> <br /> Only one of my players has really gone all in on their artifact so far but I'm thinking the others will soon.<br /> <br /> I actually love Artifacts and often make them for my group's pcs and NPCs, though they aren't often invested in as much as I do.<br /> <br /> My Dawn also has a cursed sword he bargins evocations from but those are more rough draft powers that I don't know much about and he's not willing to let it off the leash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T09:44:34-07:00","id":1340040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1339715#post1339715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm not sure if this counts, but I once had one of my player's Dawns challenge a powerful Dragonblooded queen to a duel and by the grace of Shining Ice Mirror she actually won</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen it used by a DB vs a Lunar. I wouldn't say she'd have won if it wasn't for her mates helping her, but Winter-Night Cut followed by Ice-Fixing Strike really nerfed him. He already had -1 Defence from DBT, so instead of a base Defence of 6 he was down to 3 (1 from DBT, 1 from Winter-Night Cut, 1 from Ice-Fixing Strike).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, it's true she was using the Solar evocations for SIM </div> </div> </div> What do you mean?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Otherwise I've had much the same experience as you, most players don't even bother with attunement bonuses from what I've seen, and I'm not sure any of them have taken evocations or made their own. </div> </div> </div>That's actually true. I think I'm literally one of only 2 players (out of... 10? Between different games) who's asked the ST for an attunement bonus.<br /> <br /> I ought to think of an attunement bonus for the Full Moon in my Lunar game, he has a Grimcleaver made of his own Walrus tusk, but I don't really have any ideas for the theme of a Moonsilver-Walrus Grimcleaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:04:00-07:00","id":1340044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340040#post1340040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What do you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sample Evocations in the Corebook for Shining Ice Mirror are explicitly not for use by Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> &quot;Below are a number of sample artifact weapons and armor, and their associated Evocations. Unless otherwise specified, these are designed for use by Solar characters, and will yield up fewer Evocations, Evocations of reduced power, or even nothing whatsoever in the hands of other sorts of characters. [...]<br /> <br /> Evocations of Shining Ice Mirror<br /> A Solar who&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:10:32-07:00","id":1340046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340040#post1340040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's actually true. I think I'm literally one of only 2 players (out of... 10? Between different games) who's asked the ST for an attunement bonus.<br /> <br /> I ought to think of an attunement bonus for the Full Moon in my Lunar game, he has a Grimcleaver made of his own Walrus tusk, but I don't really have any ideas for the theme of a Moonsilver-Walrus Grimcleaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an issue I\u2019ve had as well. When everyone has a pair of artifacts, thinking up ten attunement bonuses that are good enough to be useful while not being mechanically broken, and starting on the path for a unique and cool theme for their weapon/armor, it\u2019s iust hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:21:56-07:00","id":1340051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340046#post1340046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an issue I\u2019ve had as well. When everyone has a pair of artifacts, thinking up ten attunement bonuses that are good enough to be useful while not being mechanically broken, and starting on the path for a unique and cool theme for their weapon/armor, it\u2019s iust hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah same problem here. I hope in my future campaign where I can have 2 or 3 players I'll have more design space to think of that and encourage them to take artifacts with Evocations","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:36:19-07:00","id":1340053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340044#post1340044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sample Evocations in the Corebook for Shining Ice Mirror are explicitly not for use by Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> &quot;Below are a number of sample artifact weapons and armor, and their associated Evocations. Unless otherwise specified, these are designed for use by Solar characters, and will yield up fewer Evocations, Evocations of reduced power, or even nothing whatsoever in the hands of other sorts of characters. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I assumed that was essentially the early form of Resonant/Dissonant. That's how I run it.<br /> <br /> Ie a Dragonblood gets Evocations of the same power (mostly the same, but obviously they'll have something different to the ones that have Solar charms as prerequisites) as a Solar when wielding Shining Ice Mirror, Spring Razor or Volcano Cutter; while a Lunar gets slightly weaker charms, and a Sidereal weaker still, and they may not be able to access the final charm. Similarly, a Lunar gets the same evocations with Moonlit Huntress as a Solar and everyone else less, a Sidereal gets the same evocations with Freedom's Cadence as a Solar but everyone else less, and an Abyssal gets the same evocations with Black Wind as a Solar and everyone else less.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it just doesn't fit with the rules in all the rest of the books. (Obviously that's because it was written before those had been fully fleshed out, but that seems the obvious way to square that circle).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:38:23-07:00","id":1340054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340046#post1340046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an issue I\u2019ve had as well. When everyone has a pair of artifacts, thinking up ten attunement bonuses that are good enough to be useful while not being mechanically broken, and starting on the path for a unique and cool theme for their weapon/armor, it\u2019s iust hard.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't even have that many and it's difficult. In my Lunar game, one PC has a Moonsilver Grimcleaver and one a Moonsilver powerbow. They did pick up some Jade artefacts (Rainwalker, which works fine for Lunars, and a suit of red jade samurai armour) from Dragonblood they killed, but they traded them back as part of a peace agreement. I didn't think of attunement bonuses for the Dragonblood's artefacts either.<br /> <br /> I'll be honest, occasionally players think of a cool thing with their artefact weapon (for example, the Full Moon with the grimcleaver made of his own tusk) but a lot of the time they take it because they have the merit dots and don't really put any thought into it. Which is hardly inspiring when it comes to thinking of evocation sets.<br /> <br /> (I've actually just had a thought for the Walrus-axe; maybe it could turn into a silver tusk in his mouth again when he takes Walrus form, allowing him to still attack with it, or something like that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-07-2019, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T10:45:56-07:00","id":1340057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340053#post1340053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll be honest, I assumed that was essentially the early form of Resonant/Dissonant. That's how I run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is, some artifacts are clearly meant to work like that. Spring Razor specifies that it may be used by Solars or Dragon-Blooded whilst SIM and Volcano Cutter specifically state they're for Solars (and the fluff around Volcano Cutter strongly suggests it's not for Deebs).<br /> <br /> Nothing wrong with your approach. (Because it's basically Vance's approach and it's logical.) But later artifacts gatekeep powerful Evocations behind native prereqs whilst the Corebook Evocations rely on the blanket disclaimer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T13:04:48-07:00","id":1340070,"title":"","content":"I've purchased two Evocations for the Raiton Regalia, a four-dot suit of light artifact armor; one lets me make a free threaten roll the first time I take a non-trivial enemy out from stealth in a scene, while the other adds my threshold successes on a rush to the withering damage roll when I attack my quarry. Other Evocations I intend to take will make the time to switch personas as Knight Raiton occur more quickly. I only recently acquired it, so I haven't had much chance to play around with it.<br /> <br /> \u200bOther PCs in my group have Artifacts as well, but I'm not as familiar with their sheets, so I won't discuss them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T14:53:57-07:00","id":1340092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1339693-what-artefacts-have-you-taken-what-fun-did-you-have-with-their-evocations?p=1340057#post1340057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But later artifacts gatekeep powerful Evocations behind native prereqs whilst the Corebook Evocations rely on the blanket disclaimer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I'm only about 90% sure what you're saying here, so could you say a bit more about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've purchased two Evocations for the Raiton Regalia, a four-dot suit of light artifact armor; one lets me make a free threaten roll the first time I take a non-trivial enemy out from stealth in a scene,ther Evocations I intend to take will make the time to switch personas as Knight Raiton occur more quickly.<br /> I've purchased two Evocations for the Raiton Regalia, a four-dot suit of light artifact armor; one lets me make a free threaten roll the first time I take a non-trivial enemy out from stealth in a scene... other Evocations I intend to take will make the time to switch personas as Knight Raiton occur more quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like these.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just not very confident writing my own charms, or checking charms my players write for themselves, etc, etc. I always want to port an already written evocation set or something, but sometimes, well... it just doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe Exigents will help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-07-2019, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T19:31:02-07:00","id":1340135,"title":"","content":"In games I've been in:<br /> I played a sorcerer who built up evocations off of a spell (Stoking the fires to a higher temperature with each strike), evocations were the character's primary combat charms. I ended up not using this much before I swapped out the character due to party conflict issues.<br /> <br /> In games I've run:<br /> One player had a ton of fun with volcano cutter and trying to get it to actually be useful, He only really managed it twice, but he had fun with it.<br /> One player built up a custom series of evocations around an Infinite Jade Chakram that they took from an immaculate sent to kill them. They had a couple of weird effects from it, the only one I really remember (this was several years ago now) was the ability to use it as a form of movement and throw it to yourself.<br /> <br /> Most of my players were not really excited about evocations and just wanted artifacts for the functionality and/or stat boosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-07T22:51:14-07:00","id":1340163,"title":"","content":"One thing i have toyed with is making an artifact for the first 2e character i ever played - the blood ape familiar of the circle's Twilight, that later on died in a major battle and was brought back in upgraded form, with ghost, fae &amp; elemental parts mixed in, through the wonders of Ephemeral Induction Technique.<br /> <br /> I had some fun with roleplaying Gaogai's adaptation process to the change of capacities, identity &amp; function (the Twilight found her new bodyguard too pleasing to the eye to use as <b><i>just </i></b>a meatshield), fragments of memories of past selves and toyed a bit with him developing new charms and other stuff from remnants of its past selves or equipment.<br /> <br /> One of those things blending themes of ghost and demon that i have imagined was a war drum/gong/shield mixing themes from the Second-Shadow Drum with Irenio\u2019s Bell (obviously without the evocations with Solar charm requisites), both from Arms of Chosen.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the matter if artifact/evocation development in game, much like with <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/116419-giving-the-little-guy-some-room-to-shine-first-circle-demons-as-individuals\">demons or elementals at play</a>, i would say it's wait and see. You throw a lure on their way - like an antagonist using some basic evocation of the artifact before the PC acquires it, or the exalt having a past life vision related to manifesting an evocation of its own - just to see how they react, if that piques or not their interest.<br /> <br /> But let their input dictate your degree of investment. Remember you'll have a circle, meaning that between loot from fighting dynasts (or lunars, spirits, fae or the threat of the ST's choice) and whatever they picked on their backstory with merits dots you might easily end up with 5-10 artifacts at the table in the first half dozen sections. Trying to give a complete Arms-style entry for each of them - who wants that, specially for the PCs to just trade with the first potential ally they find or throw it iunder the sofa and forget?<br /> <br /> Keep things minimal. Do - or steal (no shame in that, many things can start from common ground and then spin wholy different paths) - one evocation for each, one sentence or two of artifact backstory (ancient heirloom, nameless treasure found in a ruin, brand new wonder made by mystery power who might want the investment back, etc) just to test how they answer and leave investment for those who show an interest on investing on that niche.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-26-2019, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}